  "question": {
    "text": "An object is kept at a distance of 16 cm from a thin lens and the image formed is real. If the object is kept at a distance of 6 cm from the same lens, the image formed is virtual. If the sizes of the images formed are equal the focal length of the lens will be"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "21 cm",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "11 cm",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "15 cm",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "17 cm",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "B"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "As a convex lens alone can form a real images as well as a virtual images, therefore, the lens in the present question is a convex lens. Let <math><mi>f</mi></math> be the focal length of the lens and <math><mi>m</mi></math> be the magnification produced<br/><br/>In the first case, when image is real,<br/><br/><math><mi>u</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>16</mn><mi> </mi></math>cm,<math><mi> </mi><mi>v</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>×</mo><mn>16</mn><mo>)</mo></math>cm<br/><br/>As  <math><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>v</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>u</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi></mrow></mfrac></math><br/><br/><math><mo>∴</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>16</mn><mi>m</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>16</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi></mrow></mfrac><mi> </mi><mi> </mi></math>or<math><mi> </mi><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>16</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi></mrow></mfrac><mi> </mi><mi> </mi></math>...(i)<br/><br/>In the second case, when image is virtual<br/><br/><math><mi>u</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>6</mn><mi> </mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>(</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>6</mn><mi> </mi></math>m)cm<br/><br/>From  <math><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>v</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>u</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi></mrow></mfrac></math><br/><br/><math><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>6</mn><mi>m</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>6</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi></mrow></mfrac><mi> </mi><mi> </mi></math>or<math><mi> </mi><mi> </mi><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>6</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi></mrow></mfrac></math>,  ...(ii)<br/><br/>Add Eq.(i) and Eq.(ii) we have<br/><br/><math><mn>2</mn><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>22</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi></mrow></mfrac><mi> </mi><mi> </mi></math>or<math><mi> </mi><mi> </mi><mi>f</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>22</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>11</mn><mi> </mi></math>cm"
  }
}